Build @opentui/core's native library on FreeBSD.

opentui's Zig build refuses to build for the host unless the host appears in
its SUPPORTED_TARGETS table:

  No matching supported target for native platform (x86_64-freebsd)
  error: UnsupportedNativeTarget

Two additions are enough — nothing in the Zig or C/C++ sources needed
touching:

  1. FreeBSD entries in SUPPORTED_TARGETS (x86_64 and aarch64; the aarch64 one
     is untested here, it is listed so the Chimp/aarch64 target is not blocked
     on a second patch).
  2. A .freebsd arm in the linkSystemLibraries() switch. It omits the "dl"
     that the Linux arm links, because on FreeBSD dlopen(3) and friends live
     in libc and there is no separate libdl to link; libm and libpthread (a
     filter over libthr) are real and are linked as on Linux.

ghosttyVtAvailable() is deliberately left alone: it returns false for FreeBSD
via its `else` arm, so the ghostty-vt terminal emulator is compiled out. That
is what the RC=0 build below actually built — whether opentui needs it at
runtime for opencode's TUI has NOT been verified.

Verified on a FreeBSD build host ( FreeBSD 15.1-RC2, zig 0.16.0, opentui @ main,
packages/native version 0.1.11): `sh scripts/prepare-zig-deps.sh` then
`zig build -Doptimize=ReleaseFast` exits 0 and produces
lib/x86_64-freebsd/libopentui.so — 20 MB, 1829 exported text symbols.

--- a/packages/native/build.zig	2026-08-26 13:45:50.847520000 +0000
+++ b/packages/native/build.zig	2026-08-26 13:45:50.865680000 +0000
@@ -25,6 +25,8 @@
     .{ .zig_target = "aarch64-linux-musl", .output_name = "aarch64-linux-musl", .description = "Linux aarch64 (musl)" },
     .{ .zig_target = "x86_64-macos.13.0", .output_name = "x86_64-macos", .description = "macOS x86_64 (Intel)" },
     .{ .zig_target = "aarch64-macos.13.0", .output_name = "aarch64-macos", .description = "macOS aarch64 (Apple Silicon)" },
+    .{ .zig_target = "x86_64-freebsd", .output_name = "x86_64-freebsd", .description = "FreeBSD x86_64" },
+    .{ .zig_target = "aarch64-freebsd", .output_name = "aarch64-freebsd", .description = "FreeBSD aarch64" },
     .{ .zig_target = "x86_64-windows-gnu", .output_name = "x86_64-windows", .description = "Windows x86_64" },
     .{ .zig_target = "aarch64-windows-gnu", .output_name = "aarch64-windows", .description = "Windows aarch64" },
 };
@@ -367,6 +369,10 @@
         .macos => addMacOSSystemLibraries(b, module, macos_sdk_path.?),
         .linux => {
             module.linkSystemLibrary("dl", .{});
+            module.linkSystemLibrary("pthread", .{});
+            module.linkSystemLibrary("m", .{});
+        },
+        .freebsd => {
             module.linkSystemLibrary("pthread", .{});
             module.linkSystemLibrary("m", .{});
         },
